      }","body":"<h2>Integrated Cell Browser</h2>
<p style="font-size:18px;">Explore interactive visualizations of single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) and single-nucleus ATAC-seq (snATAC-seq) data from pancreatic islet cells.</p>
<p>Three major maps are currently available:</p>
<p>1. Single cell expression map of pancreatic islets using data from 65 human donors sourced from <a href="/hpap-program.html" target="blank">HPAP</a> (scRNA-seq)</p>
<p>2. Integrated single cell expression map of pancreatic islets using data from 140 human donors sourced from <a href="/hpap-program.html" target="blank">HPAP</a>, <a href="/iidp-program.html" target="blank">IIDP</a>, and <a href="/prodo-program.html" target="blank">Prodo</a> (scRNA-seq)</p>
<p>3. Single cell chromatin accessibility map of pancreatic islets using data from 41 human donors sourced from <a href="/hpap-program.html" target="blank">HPAP</a> (snATAC-seq)</p>
<p>Within a selected dataset, visualize interactive plots of cell type clusters, gene expression, cell type abundance, and marker gene expression. Query a gene name and filter results using the desired parameters. <span style="color:#f47920;"><strong>Please be patient, as data may take some time to load.</strong></span>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Detailed data processing methods are available for <a href="https://data.pankbase.org/method/scprocessing_v1" target="blank">v1</a> and <a href="https://data.pankbase.org/method/scprocessing_v3pt3" target="blank">v3.3</a> of the integrated single cell expression map of pancreatic islets using data from HPAP, IIDP and Prodo. Descriptions are available <a href="https://hugeampkpncms.org/sites/default/files/images/pankbase/methods/SCB_traitdescription.pdf" target="blank">here</a> for traits that can be used to stratify cell count and gene expression plots.</p>
<p>Explore the underlying <a href="https://data.pankbase.org" target="blank">donor data</a>, <a href="https://pankbase.org/donor-metadata.html" target="blank">donor metadata</a>, and <a href="/metadata-data-standards.html" target="blank">data and metadata standards</a>. Find quantitative trait loci (QTLs) of the queried gene through <a href="https://pankgraph.org" target="blank">PanKgraph</a>.</p>
<p>If you use data from this page, please review our <a href="/policies.html" target="blank">Citation Policies</a> to ensure proper citation of the underlying resource(s) used to generate these maps.</p>
